<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Udaipur State (Chhattisgarh)</h1><p class="st-meta">1818 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Dharamjaigarh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A forested feudatory state of northern Chhattisgarh, ruled from Dharamjaigarh by a branch of the house of Sarguja.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a> was a dependency of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/surguja-state">Sarguja</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chota-nagpur-plateau">Chota Nagpur</a> hills and came under British supervision around 1818 with the other states taken from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nagpur-kingdom">Nagpur Kingdom</a>. Its ruler was deprived of the state in the 1850s, and it was regranted to a branch of the Sarguja family in 1860.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state was hilly, forested and largely Adivasi, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurukh-people">Oraon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kawar-people">Kanwar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gond-people">Gond</a> communities. It belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chota-nagpur-plateau">Chota Nagpur</a> tributary states and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh-feudatory-states">Chhattisgarh States</a> group of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-states-agency">Eastern States Agency</a>, ruled by a Raja from Dharamjaigarh.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a> acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and on 1 January 1948 was merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces and Berar</a>. Its lands are now in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/raigarh-state">Raigarh</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="princely state, 1818 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">princely state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Indian princely states</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.88%;width:2.59%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1818 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dharamjaigarh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism; Adivasi traditions</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Chhattisgarhi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dharamjaigarh</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1883&amp;focus=udaipur-state-chhattisgarh" aria-label="Udaipur State (Chhattisgarh) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6907 1348 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Udaipur State (Chhattisgarh) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7227 1604L7364 1602M7227 1604L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7227 1604h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7227 1604h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dharamjaigarh. <a href="/atlas?year=1883&amp;focus=udaipur-state-chhattisgarh">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
